The Russian United Social Democratic Party (ROSDP) was a short-lived Russian center-left political party led by Mikhail Gorbachev, the former president of the USSR. The party included representatives on an individual basis:

- the Social Democrats movement;
- Social Democratic Union;
- The Russian Democratic Reform Movement;
- Social Liberal Party of Russia;
- the New Left movement;
- Labor Party, etc.

In 2001, the party merged with the RPSD in the Social Democratic Party of Russia

